# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Poids de modèles — plusieurs dizaines de Go, jamais dans git.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/models/
# Served GGUFs. The first name is the directory this deployment still has
# on disk (47 GB): renaming the RULE without moving the DIRECTORY is how
# 47 GB becomes visible to `git add -A`. The second is where the server
# layout puts them.
/edgem-gguf/
/models/gguf/

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Environnements virtuels Python.
# spear est à la fois l'application ET son venv : le code est versionné,
# l'arborescence du venv ne l'est pas (5,4 Go).
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/spear/bin/
/spear/include/
/spear/lib/
/spear/lib64
/spear/share/
/spear/pyvenv.cfg
/qwen3-finetune/.venv/

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Caches reconstructibles : index vectoriel (index_corpus.py) et cache
# HuggingFace datasets du fine-tuning (fichiers .arrow, répertoires hachés).
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/spear/chromadb/
/qwen3-finetune/models/datasets/

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Données d'exécution : transcriptions de conversation et journal d'audit.
# Elles grossissent à chaque session et figeraient le contenu des échanges
# dans l'historique git. Le code qui les produit est versionné, lui.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/spear/history*.json
/spear/history*.jsonl
/spear/audit/
/spear/standards/
# Canonical training episodes/drafts are local evidence and may contain
# redacted task content.  Keep this explicit even though audit/ is ignored.
/spear/audit/training-data/
/spear/llama-server.log
/spear/.input_history

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Clone upstream de llama.cpp : porte son propre dépôt git (ggml-org/llama.cpp)
# et son répertoire de build.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/llama.cpp-next/

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Sorties générées.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/doc/build/
# Rendered PNGs: export_png.sh makes them from the tracked SVGs on demand, for
# a slide or an issue. The SVG is the artifact worth versioning -- it is what
# the documentation embeds, and it stays crisp at any zoom.
/doc/source/img/*.png
# The logotype is not one of them: it is a source asset, not a render of a
# tracked SVG, and nothing in the tree can reproduce it. Excluded by default
# and re-admitted by name, so a rendered PNG dropped here tomorrow still does
# not enter by oversight.
!/doc/source/img/REDS-HEIG-VD.png
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo

# État runtime : dernier backend choisi, réécrit à chaque lancement.
/spear/active-backend.conf

# GPU epingle sur machine partagee — voir embedding.py
/spear/active-gpu.conf
# reglages d'endpoint propres a la machine — voir spear-chat.sh
/spear/machine.env

# Backend endpoints: a host, a user and a key path, per machine and per
# rental. The tracked *.example files carry the schema and nothing else.
/spear/reds.conf
/spear/reds.local.conf
/spear/pod.conf

# Per-machine configuration: these hold ABSOLUTE paths, so tracking them means
# every sync overwrites the target machine's settings with the author's. That
# is exactly what happened on reds-ml — a git reset --hard silently repointed
# all 15 corpora at /home/operator paths that do not exist there, and at a
# model file on the wrong host. See projects.example.json for the schema.
/spear/projects.json
/spear/active-model.conf

# GPU offload target for indexing — per machine, holds an ssh destination
/spear/active-embed-remote.conf

# …and the command that runs the worker THERE. Per machine for the same
# reason: it is the remote account's directory layout, which the tracked code
# deliberately knows nothing about. See reds.conf.example for the shape.
/spear/active-embed-remote-cmd.conf

# A real server deployment config placed in the checkout instead of
# ~/spear-runtime/config/. It names one machine -- host, card, model paths --
# and server/config/ ships only *.example on purpose. Ignored so that putting
# it here by mistake cannot become a commit.
/server/config/server.conf
/server/config/gpu.conf
/server/config/*.local.conf

# Build output, not source: docker/gen-registry.py regenerates it from this
# machine's projects.json on every docker/build.sh run. A committed copy is
# one machine's corpus graph — names, federations and collection hashes —
# published for no benefit, and stale the moment a corpus is added.
/docker/projects.docker.json
